   "subject": "grouping behavior in dplyr",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m seeing odd behavior applying dplyr verbs - arrange, for one - to a grouped data_frame.  At first, I thought it was related to a variable transformed by lubridate, but maybe it&#39;s something fundamental about grouping that I fail to grasp:<div><br></div><div>eg, given</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dplyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data_frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qual </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;B&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dates </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2014-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2014-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>the following fails to correctly arrange:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>creating the variable earlier in the pipe chain via mutate likewise fails:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>note that the class() of the above output is:</div><div><br></div><div>[1] &quot;grouped_df&quot; &quot;tbl_df&quot;     &quot;tbl&quot;        &quot;data.frame&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>if we re-convert the output to a df at the end of the pipe (which I think is equivalent to ungroup()), it works:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><b><span style=\"color:#000\">as_data_frame</span></b><b><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></b><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Is this a feature or a bug?  Any guidance from this fine community is appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div> </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Vb5tGKP3CgAJ",
   "from": "Doug Mitarotonda",
   "author": "9c9b5f9c6aaa025d",
   "date": "2015-10-02T17:44:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: grouping behavior in dplyr",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>What do you mean by “fails to correctly arrange?” Do you mean that you want the arranging to be on the full data frame, not the groups? If so, then, as you alluded to, use `ungroup` and get that result. </div><div><br></div><div>In your “failed” example, you are grouping the data, summarizing within that grouping, and then arranging within that grouping. That is a perfectly reasonable thing to do even if it is not what you are trying to do. To get what you want, you need to group the data, summarize within that grouping, remove the grouping of data (i.e., use `ungroup`), and then arrange the entire data frame. </div><div><br></div><div>&gt; xyz %&gt;% group_by(qual, yr = lubridate::year(dates)) %&gt;% summarise(qty = sum(qty)) %&gt;% ungroup() %&gt;% arrange(yr)</div><div>Source: local data frame [4 x 3]</div><div><br></div><div>   qual    yr   qty</div><div>  (chr) (dbl) (int)</div><div>1     B  2014     5</div><div>2     C  2014     3</div><div>3     A  2015     3</div><div>4     C  2015     4 </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Oct 2, 2015, at 10:08 AM, ArjunaCap &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mcaw...@greenstenergy.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m seeing odd behavior applying dplyr verbs - arrange, for one - to a grouped data_frame.  At first, I thought it was related to a variable transformed by lubridate, but maybe it&#39;s something fundamental about grouping that I fail to grasp:<div><br></div><div>eg, given</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>dplyr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br>xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> data_frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qual </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;B&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> dates </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2014-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2014-05-01&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>the following fails to correctly arrange:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span>xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span>year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>creating the variable earlier in the pipe chain via mutate likewise fails:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span>xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span>year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>note that the class() of the above output is:</div><div><br></div><div>[1] &quot;grouped_df&quot; &quot;tbl_df&quot;     &quot;tbl&quot;        &quot;data.frame&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>if we re-convert the output to a df at the end of the pipe (which I think is equivalent to ungroup()), it works:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span>xyz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> mutate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>yr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> lubridate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span>year</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>dates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> group_by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> summarise</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>qty</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> </span><b><span>as_data_frame</span></b><b><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></b><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span> arrange</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>yr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Is this a feature or a bug?  Any guidance from this fine community is appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div> </div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
